Well, I'm glad

00:16:44.087 --> 00:16:47.257
that you're safe.

00:16:47.257 --> 00:16:48.675
Hey, weird question.

00:16:48.675 --> 00:16:50.761
Why did you drive three miles

00:16:48.675 --> 00:16:50.761
down Route 23

00:16:50.761 --> 00:16:52.804
and take a pee behind

00:16:50.761 --> 00:16:52.804
a convenience store?

00:16:52.804 --> 00:16:56.015
Okay, I'll tell you,

00:16:52.804 --> 00:16:56.015
but before I do, promise me

00:16:56.015 --> 00:16:58.560
that we are not gonna move to

00:16:56.015 --> 00:16:58.560
St. Cloud, Minnesota. Promise.

00:16:58.560 --> 00:17:01.312
I'm not suggesting that we move

00:16:58.560 --> 00:17:01.312
here tomorrow, I'm just...

00:17:01.312 --> 00:17:02.564
Promise.

00:17:02.564 --> 00:17:03.815
Why do you want me

00:17:02.564 --> 00:17:03.815
to promise you that?

00:17:03.815 --> 00:17:05.567
Because I don't

00:17:03.815 --> 00:17:05.567
fit in here.

00:17:05.567 --> 00:17:07.110
I'm not eight feet tall,

00:17:07.110 --> 00:17:08.695
and I don't think

00:17:07.110 --> 00:17:08.695
you could call it a salad

00:17:08.695 --> 00:17:10.781
if it has Funyuns in it.

00:17:10.781 --> 00:17:12.323
I'm<i> Funyuns.</i>

00:17:12.323 --> 00:17:15.535
And mayonnaise and gummi bears

00:17:12.323 --> 00:17:15.535
and bask-ice-ball,

00:17:15.535 --> 00:17:17.036
and I love St. Cloud.

00:17:17.036 --> 00:17:18.663
And, yes, there is a part of me

00:17:18.663 --> 00:17:20.373
that would like

00:17:18.663 --> 00:17:20.373
to move here someday,

00:17:20.373 --> 00:17:22.083
and why are we

00:17:20.373 --> 00:17:22.083
having this discussion

00:17:22.083 --> 00:17:25.211
in a jail cell on Thanksgiving?

00:17:25.211 --> 00:17:27.380
Okay, personal effects.

00:17:27.380 --> 00:17:28.381
One wallet.

00:17:28.381 --> 00:17:29.424
One cell phone.

00:17:29.424 --> 00:17:33.177
One... pregnancy test.

00:17:40.184 --> 00:17:42.646
Pete arrested me

00:17:40.184 --> 00:17:42.646
before I could look at it.

00:17:50.821 --> 00:17:51.905
Whoa.

00:17:51.905 --> 00:17:53.406
Yeah.

00:17:53.406 --> 00:17:57.828
Lily, we can't let our kids

00:17:53.406 --> 00:17:57.828
play bask-ice-ball.

00:17:57.828 --> 00:18:01.247
Bask-ice-ball is

00:17:57.828 --> 00:18:01.247
really dangerous.

00:18:01.247 --> 00:18:03.374
Yeah, what are the rules

00:18:01.247 --> 00:18:03.374
to that game anyway?

00:18:03.374 --> 00:18:04.375
There are no rules.

00:18:04.375 --> 00:18:08.212
We just whale

00:18:04.375 --> 00:18:08.212
on each other.

00:18:11.174 --> 00:18:14.719
Look, I don't want to be

00:18:11.174 --> 00:18:14.719
exactly like my family.

00:18:15.929 --> 00:18:18.181
And don't take this

00:18:15.929 --> 00:18:18.181
the wrong way,

00:18:18.181 --> 00:18:21.893
but I don't want to be

00:18:18.181 --> 00:18:21.893
exactly like your family either.

00:18:23.311 --> 00:18:25.355
We'll be our own family.

00:18:25.355 --> 00:18:29.818
And we'll find our own way

00:18:25.355 --> 00:18:29.818
to freak out the people

00:18:29.818 --> 00:18:31.152
our kids bring home.

00:18:34.280 --> 00:18:36.449
Great, now I'm crying.

00:18:36.449 --> 00:18:38.117
Look.

00:18:38.117 --> 00:18:40.453
We may have some really

00:18:38.117 --> 00:18:40.453
big decisions to make

00:18:40.453 --> 00:18:42.789
in about ten seconds.

00:18:42.789 --> 00:18:44.123
But right now,

00:18:44.123 --> 00:18:45.792
I don't care where

00:18:44.123 --> 00:18:45.792
our kids grow up,

00:18:45.792 --> 00:18:48.419
as long as they have

00:18:45.792 --> 00:18:48.419
you for a father.

00:18:51.589 --> 00:18:54.133
Gosh, I hope

00:18:51.589 --> 00:18:54.133
you're the father.

00:18:54.133 --> 00:18:57.554
Just a little joke to

00:18:54.133 --> 00:18:57.554
lighten up the mood.

00:19:01.933 --> 00:19:03.101
What does it say?

00:19:03.101 --> 00:19:05.770
I'm afraid to look.

00:19:05.770 --> 00:19:07.438
PETE:

00:19:05.770 --> 00:19:07.438
It's negative!

00:19:07.438 --> 00:19:09.900
Oh, thank God.

00:19:09.900 --> 00:19:11.359
Oh, thank God.

00:19:12.402 --> 00:19:14.362
And, hey!

00:19:16.155 --> 00:19:19.117
Ted. Are you listening?

00:19:19.117 --> 00:19:20.994
You're a good guy.

00:19:20.994 --> 00:19:22.662
Want to know why I

00:19:20.994 --> 00:19:22.662
have to work tomorrow?

00:19:22.662 --> 00:19:24.039
My firm's designing

00:19:24.039 --> 00:19:26.750
an executive lounge

00:19:24.039 --> 00:19:26.750
for a tobacco company.

00:19:26.750 --> 00:19:29.669
In the fight against cancer,

00:19:26.750 --> 00:19:29.669
I'm on the side of cancer.

00:19:29.669 --> 00:19:31.295
BARNEY: Okay,

00:19:29.669 --> 00:19:31.295
Ted, I found

00:19:31.295 --> 00:19:32.338
a way for you

00:19:31.295 --> 00:19:32.338
to help someone.

00:19:32.338 --> 00:19:33.297
To do some good.

00:19:33.297 --> 00:19:34.298
This is Walter.

00:19:34.298 --> 00:19:35.717
Walter is homeless.

00:19:35.717 --> 00:19:38.302
And Walter would

00:19:35.717 --> 00:19:38.302
like a lap dance.

00:19:38.302 --> 00:19:40.097
Are you joking?

00:19:40.097 --> 00:19:44.225
I never joke about the sublime

00:19:40.097 --> 00:19:44.225
art of burlesque entertainment.

00:19:44.225 --> 00:19:46.477
No, Barney, that's insane.

00:19:46.477 --> 00:19:49.272
Sir, would you like me to buy

00:19:46.477 --> 00:19:49.272
you a ticket to the buffet?

00:19:49.272 --> 00:19:51.024
No, I'm stuffed.

00:19:51.024 --> 00:19:53.359
Just a lap dance

00:19:51.024 --> 00:19:53.359
will be fine.

00:19:53.359 --> 00:19:55.904
Ted, Walter's been to

00:19:53.359 --> 00:19:55.904
three shelter dinners.

00:19:55.904 --> 00:19:57.196
You know where

00:19:55.904 --> 00:19:57.196
he hasn't been?

00:19:57.196 --> 00:20:00.408
To heaven

00:19:57.196 --> 00:20:00.408
with Samantha.

00:20:00.408 --> 00:20:03.411
Look, it's the one chance

00:20:00.408 --> 00:20:03.411
you've had all day

00:20:03.411 --> 00:20:04.704
to help someone

00:20:03.411 --> 00:20:04.704
in need.

00:20:04.704 --> 00:20:06.581
Now, buy this man

00:20:04.704 --> 00:20:06.581
a lap dance.

00:20:06.581 --> 00:20:11.502
You said you wanted to see the

00:20:06.581 --> 00:20:11.502
look of joy in someone's eyes.

00:20:11.502 --> 00:20:15.048
You know, I don't think

00:20:11.502 --> 00:20:15.048
I'm going to watch.

00:20:16.007 --> 00:20:18.176
Here you go, Walter.

00:20:18.176 --> 00:20:19.719
Happy Thanksgiving.

00:20:19.719 --> 00:20:22.472
Thank you so much.

00:20:22.472 --> 00:20:24.766
No, really. Thank you.

00:20:28.186 --> 00:20:30.147
Happy Thanksgiving, guys.

00:20:31.856 --> 00:20:34.358
Thanksgiving in November.

00:20:34.358 --> 00:20:35.735
Weird.

00:20:37.695 --> 00:20:41.616
(<i> slow-tempo</i> ): ♪ I treat it

00:20:37.695 --> 00:20:41.616
like a high school dance ♪

00:20:41.616 --> 00:20:44.661
TED:

00:20:41.616 --> 00:20:44.661
<i>So, that was Thanksgiving 2005.</i>

00:20:44.661 --> 00:20:46.704
<i>To be honest,</i>

00:20:44.661 --> 00:20:46.704
<i>it didn't go great.</i>

00:20:46.704 --> 00:20:48.665
<i>But life has</i>

00:20:46.704 --> 00:20:48.665
<i>plenty of good parts,</i>

00:20:48.665 --> 00:20:50.708
<i>it's the rough parts</i>

00:20:48.665 --> 00:20:50.708
<i>that make you thankful</i>

00:20:50.708 --> 00:20:52.836
<i>you have people</i>

00:20:50.708 --> 00:20:52.836
<i>to share it with.</i>

00:20:52.836 --> 00:20:55.630
♪ ...Stare at my shoes ♪

00:20:55.630 --> 00:20:58.299
♪ You belong to me ♪

00:20:58.299 --> 00:21:00.969
♪ I belong to you ♪

00:21:06.557 --> 00:21:10.687
♪ I could tell

00:21:06.557 --> 00:21:10.687
